BLOCK exact successor 120e5202148e7a8703625f00474cc310f2d7ac40.

The production parser now rejects missing, empty, non-string, tabbed, or multiline OID, candidate ID, and phase fields. The exact committed court passes; bash -n and diff-check are clean; the author receipt hash matches f447100809f66b2f277f687b36d1f41aed31c4ae6eb39a6a057e9350ed6d2163. In a scratch exact-SHA export, additional current-code probes for empty candidate ID, missing OID, and a valid landed row beside a malformed row all exit 3.

The durable court is still incomplete against the acceptance condition in my predecessor review. It adds only the single missing-candidate-ID row. I changed the parser in reviewer scratch from raising on an invalid identity row to continuing past it. Under that mutation:

- the committed premerge-check-test.sh still passes;
- a list containing one valid landed row followed by one row missing candidate_id exits 0;
- the gate prints the valid row as reconciled and reports Mechanical checks passed;
- the requested mixed-row court fails with expected exit 3, got 0.

That is the partial-parser-output failure the prior review explicitly required a malformed-row-beside-valid-row court to prevent. A future per-row skip can restore the gate bypass while every committed test remains green.

Required successor: keep the current production rejection, and commit an exact-exit-3 court containing a valid landed row plus a malformed identity row. Also complete the previously requested empty-candidate-ID court; a missing-OID court is appropriate because the successor now claims all three identity coordinates are required.

No candidate source was edited. Reviewer-only mutations and extra courts are under /private/tmp/storymodel4s-premerge-rereview.bmwmFz.
